# Deliberately empty. conftest.py points TSG_ENV_FILE at this file so that Settings() resolves to
# the DOCUMENTED DEFAULTS during a test run instead of reading the developer's own .env.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Settings bakes `env_file` into model_config at import time, and .env is a
# real, machine-local config that is not in git. Without this, every test that reaches production
# code took whatever that machine happened to have set: the suite was green in CI (no .env) and red
# locally on TSG_CONTROL_MAP_BACKFILL_MIN_SCORE, a DEPRECATED override this machine still enabled.
# The failing direction was the cheap one — the expensive direction is a test PASSING locally for a
# reason no test declares, which nothing would ever have reported.
#
# A test that needs a setting sets it explicitly (monkeypatch.setenv, or Settings(field=...)). That
# is the point: configuration a test depends on should be visible in the test.
#
# Do not add values here. A value in this file is ambient config again, just relocated.
